{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794327310,"nonce":"+9fSXtuLQy9bkUcvMlQ65ZtQyd8=","message":"Found while porting sdf_3d to russl: the copies had already diverged. sdf_3d.wgsl's calculate_clip_alpha used sd_rounded_rect for a rect clip (circular corners), while sdf_core.wgsl used sd_shaped_rect with clip_corner_shape, so a squircle overflow clip on a 3D primitive was clipped with circular corners. The russl port keeps the 3D behaviour by passing a constant corner shape of 1.0 to the shared calculate_clip_alpha (pixel-identical in the parity test). Whether 3D primitives should honour clip_corner_shape is open; passing prim.clip_corner_shape in sdf_3d.rs would do it.","files":null}]}